But, the archon can surround the hero with nasties before being able
to engage it in melee, or even before it can be targeted on an
orthogonal.  And once surrounded, thrown weapons won't make it through
the crowds.

Also it's difficult to melee an archon, or even throw anything at
them, accurately without a blindfold/towel and that carries the risk
of being surrounded by non-mind monsters such as iron golems, or green
slimes.  Bad still is being blind while next to a cockatrice as
killing it may or may not leave a corpse and the only way to find out
is to remove the blindfold and to do so quickly before a monster with
gloves picks the corpse up.  (The Eyes of the Overworld obviously
mitigate the blinding/stunning effects)
